Unless `compat` is computed incorrectly: `compat = {a: {b for b in names if b != a and not (file_ids.get(a, set()) & file_ids.get(b, set()))} ...}`. For files with EMPTY id sets (enrichment.csv has 0 citation ids), `file_ids.get(a, set())` = empty set → intersection empty → compat includes everything. So empty-id files are "disjoint" from everyone, and they contribute rows (39) with no ids. That's the flaw: a file with zero citation ids cannot be part of a "disjoint citation union" because its rows aren't accounted for by ids; the union size test fails, but the search never checks union size — it just assumed pairwise disjoint ⟹ union size == sum, which is FALSE when files contain non-citation rows.

